.TH SPRITESTUDIO 1 "September 2026" "SpriteStudio 0.11.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
spritestudio \- interactive 2D sprite sheet preparation, retouching, animation and game engine packing studio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spritestudio
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spritestudio
is an advanced desktop graphical workstation designed for video game creators, pixel artists, and technical animators.
It bridges the gap between raw artwork creation and game engine asset pipelines by providing:
.IP \(bu 2
Precise sprite sheet slicing with automatic connected-components edge detection and interactive boundary box manipulation.
.IP \(bu 2
Comprehensive animation management with timeline filmstrip, FPS speed control, and loop modes (Loop, Once, Ping-Pong).
.IP \(bu 2
Interactive origin and pivot alignment reticles eliminating animation jittering across variable-dimension frames.
.IP \(bu 2
A modular suite of non-destructive image filters (background removal, anti-halo despill, outline generator, color swapping, HSV adjust, pixel rescaling, and retro Bayer quantization).
.IP \(bu 2
High-density 2D atlas packing powered by MaxRects heuristics and multithreaded Tight Polygon Mesh packing (Marching Squares, RDP simplification, and Ear-Clipping triangulation saving 60% to 80% GPU overdraw).
.IP \(bu 2
A surgical pixel-by-pixel editor featuring continuous Bresenham drawing, floating clipboard stamps, dynamic palette extraction, and authentic retro hardware palettes (NES, SNES, Amiga, PC-Engine, Game Boy, PICO-8, C64).
.IP \(bu 2
Native project preservation (\fB.ssp\fR) with atomic writes, crash recovery, and integrated Git Time-Travel versioning.
.IP \(bu 2
Multi-engine exports targeting Godot 4 (\fB.tres\fR), Unity 2D (\fB.unity.json\fR), Unreal Engine Paper2D (\fB.paper2d.json\fR), TexturePacker JSON, GIF animations, and transparent PNG archives.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Display command-line help options.
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-version
Print application version and build information.
.TP
.B \-\-reset\-config
Reset application settings and user preferences stored in \fIspritestudio_config.json\fR to defaults.

.SH SUPPORTED FILE FORMATS
.SS Project Files
.TP
.B .ssp
Native SpriteStudio Project archive (compressed ZIP containing canvas textures, slice coordinates, pivots, animations, and revision snapshots).
.SS Image Formats
.TP
.B .png\fR, \fB.jpg\fR, \fB.jpeg\fR, \fB.bmp
Standard bitmap images imported as raw sprite sheets or textures.
.TP
.B .gif
Animated GIFs decoded and mapped into sequenced frames and animation tracks.
.SS Game Engine & Data Descriptors
.TP
.B .tres
Godot Engine 4 resource files (\fBSpriteFrames\fR and \fBArrayMesh\fR).
.TP
.B .json
TexturePacker and Aseprite standardized atlas descriptors (Array or Hash format).

.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open an image, sheet, or project file.
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save active \fB.ssp\fR project.
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
Open the Surgical Pixel-by-Pixel Editor.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+E
Open the Multi-Engine Export Dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y
Undo / Redo last operation.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Wheel
Smooth canvas zoom from 100% to 5000%.
.TP
.B Middle Click / Space+Drag
Pan the atlas canvas view.
.TP
.B F
Fit entire atlas in view.
.TP
.B Arrow Keys
Nudge active bounding box by 1 pixel (Shift+Arrows for 10 pixels).
.TP
.B T
Trim transparent edges on active bounding box.
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Open Background Removal filter dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P
Open MaxRects Atlas Packing filter dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+M
Open Polygon Mesh & Tight Packing dialog.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I spritestudio_config.json
Application configuration file storing user preferences, window geometries, and default tolerances.
Looked up in the local application directory first, then in \fB~/.config/SpriteStudio/\fR on Linux,
\fB~/Library/Application Support/SpriteStudio/\fR on macOS, or \fB%APPDATA%\\SpriteStudio\\\fR on Windows.

